      "note": "wake to light",
      "why": "Bed turned with its head on the east wall and its foot toward the window, so the middle of the room is one open floor. Your green VILHATTEN wardrobe fills the north-west corner facing south, with the black LACK shoe shelf beside it and clear of the door swing. Its doors open onto clear floor: the MALM tall chest starts on the west wall just past them. A ladder shelf leans on the in-push facing south, under the Capitol Reef print. Your wood nightstand stands at the head of the bed's open side. The bench sits across the foot of the bed. The snowboard hangs upright on the south wall at the window end of the bench, with its boots on a tray under it, so it sits in the dead end beside the floor lamp. No ceiling light: a floor lamp stands in the window corner, a plug-in swing-arm sconce over the bed's head corner, just above the headboard, is the reading light, and your BÖJA, Mika and PELARBOJ lamps sit on the chest, the nightstand and the top of the shoe shelf. Tightest walkway is 27 in, between the bench and the window wall; the lamp sits at its dead end.",
